Now I understand the full structure. `resolveActorFromRequest` takes `(request, db, opts)` — not just `(request, env)`. I need to pass the `db` to it.

In `app.ts`, the actor resolution is done in the main catch-all:
```typescript
app.all("/api/*", async (c) => {
  const { compiled, db, storage } = buildRequestResources(c.env);
  const actor = await resolveActorFromRequest(c.req.raw, db, { deploymentMode });
  // ...
```

For the bridge, the actor is resolved inside each route handler using the per-request DB.


