32	 * Plugin jobs are discrete units of work enqueued by the plugin job scheduler
33	 * (replaced by a Cloudflare Queue consumer on CF deployments). Each job has a
34	 * `plugin_jobs` record in the database. The Workflow:
35	 *
36	 *   1. Marks the job as "running" via the internal API.
37	 *   2. Dispatches execution to the configured executor (sandbox bridge or
38	 *      Cloudflare Container), with timeout and retry semantics.
39	 *   3. Records the outcome — success or failure — via the internal API.
40	 *
41	 * Retries up to 2 times on transient executor failures before marking the
42	 * job as permanently failed.
43	 *
44	 * Triggered by the Cloudflare Queue consumer in `api.ts` when a
45	 * `plugin_job_dispatch` message arrives on `paperclip-jobs`.
46	 */
